                            {
                                "example_id": "6f059635-098d-4e9d-bb0d-5fe10e25e629",
                                "sense_id": "2745458b-b4aa-3d2b-ad6e-7e36574a1ea8",
                                "text": "Surprisingly, Alina took banishment from Petersburg well, did not slink away to her mother in Borisoglebsk to wait for better times, but went with him to live in harsh and primitive conditions at the back of beyond, endured eighteen months of it unflinchingly, and was not too proud to cook and do the housework. He, at least, always had Schlieffen to pore over from day to day—but what had she got?"
                            }
